**Read:** [Chemical Reactor Analysis and Design Fundamentals — Rawlings and Ekerdt](../sources/Chemical-Reactor-Analysis-Rawlings-Ekerdt.lingua#r_7YQAV27Y3J0B537Z6K5HDN8H0A), the full transient, multiple-state and coupled reactor examples; [Manufacture of Organic Fine Chemicals, BREF OFC](../sources/Organic-Fine-Chemicals-BREF.lingua#r_0DH473049K4WX7HAAY1P7SDS3K), the complete relevant batch/operation and process-monitoring treatment; [Production of Chlor-alkali, BREF CAK](../sources/Chlor-Alkali-Production-BREF.lingua#r_69QNQ29VT4NA2MXHTVWDNP8T2W), the whole relevant operating, measurement and product-system context.

Process control acts on an evolving chemical/physical system through imperfect measurements and finite actuators. Temperature, pressure, composition, level and flow describe different state or output quantities. A displayed set point is not evidence that every relevant location or species is at the desired state.

Sensor dynamics, sample delays, calibration, location and fouling influence feedback. A local control loop can interact with recycles, shared utilities and another operation's constraints. Stabilizing one measured variable can conceal a changed product distribution or inventory if the observation does not capture the consequential state.

Distinguish the underlying process model, controller, operating procedure and independent protective functions. Startup, shutdown, batch transitions and disturbances require their actual time histories. A steady optimal solution may be unstable or inaccessible under the permitted actuator and measurement behavior.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete public process/control case with state, measurement and action equations. Independently check a relevant transient and compare a competing operating arrangement under changed feed or utility conditions. Explain which primary observations establish actual product/thermal behavior and which remain model predictions. Reuse the shared numerical and metrology work for error, delay and uncertainty questions.

**Continue:** [Extend a chemical process claim through scale, repeated operation and changed conditions](Scale-up-pilot-evidence-campaigns-and-process-change.lingua#r_471AV9S2RAXMYZ21KM20ESPCAC).

